# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Activity"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Direct LinkML representation of prov:Activity. Applied to events and processes that use, transform, generate, document, assess, or verify entities."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Agent"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Direct LinkML representation of prov:Agent. Agents bear responsibility for activities or entities. PROV-O permits an individual agent also to be typed as an Entity, but does not define every Agent as a subclass of Entity."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Agent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema> .
# 
# http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Entity"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Direct LinkML representation of prov:Entity. Applied to physical, digital, conceptual, and assertion-bearing things that participate in provenance relations. PROVENANCE SCOPE (design decision): for classes whose instances are real-world referents (structures, deities, places, actors), the provenance slots (was_derived_from, was_attributed_to, was_generated_by, generated_at_time) describe the DATA RECORD about the referent, not the referent itself -- a stupa is not generated by the survey that records it. Referent-level history is modelled through events (Production, DestructionEvent, etc.). RDF deployments SHOULD carry record-level provenance in named graphs or on InformationObject/Assertion nodes."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema> .
<http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Entity> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/provenance_scope> "record" .
