<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/Container> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Container"@en .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/Container> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broadMatch> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Collection> .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/Container> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Root container for cultural heritage data instances. PLACEMENT RULE: put each instance in the most specific collection available (e.g. a Festival in festivals, not ritual_events; a Person in persons, not actors); broader collections exist for instances of the general classes only."@en .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/Container> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema> .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/Container> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/design_note> "Serialization construct, not a domain class: this is the LinkML tree_root that anchors JSON/YAML dataset serializations (its collection properties exist for data exchange only). Reasoners and domain queries should ignore it; RDF instance data does not need a Container node." .
