# 
# https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/RitualAssessment> .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fearlessness Assessment"@en .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The 'fearlessness test' popularly described (animal heads, masked dancers in darkness). Its historical and contemporary practice is DISPUTED -- some former Kumaris contest how it is described. Represented as an assessment whose accounts are source-attributed via has_assertion, NOT as a mandatory criterion."@en .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/schema> .
<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/FearlessnessAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Deliberately not a SelectionCriterion subclass: popular accounts and lived testimony disagree. Attach each account as a Assertion (CRMinf I2 Belief) with its own source and confidence."@en .
